  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the value of $\\sqrt{59}\\cdot \\sqrt{59}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we re-write the expression as a square:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{59}\\cdot \\sqrt{59}={(\\sqrt{59})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\sqrt{59})}^{2}=59.\n$$",
